「唔，嗯…」%K%P
After casting a brief glance at my freshly freed leg, Toko\nwent back to her battle with the laundry.%K%P
稍稍留意了一下，\n确认我脚上终于没有再盖着臃肿的白色石膏后，\n都子便又回到了与换洗衣服之间的战斗中。%K%P
Sunday, December 16.%K%P
１２月１６日。星期天。%K%P
Seeing my right leg for the first time in a while, I\nnoticed how it shriveled up to almost half the thickness\nof my left. I found myself feeling a little dizzy as I\ngazed at them next to each other.%K%P
今天看到好久不见的右脚，\n发现跟左脚比起来显然消瘦得多，实在是让人觉得好笑。\n这样的情况让我有点眩晕。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI'll still need the crutch for a few more days, but the\ndoctor said I should be able to walk on my own by the\nweekend.\d%K%P
「然后再拄个两三天拐棍，\n到下周末之前差不多就能勉强走路了」%K%P
Although, considering the difficulties I still had with\nmoving my leg, I was beginning to question their\ndefinition of \dwalk.\d%K%P
考虑到现在如果不锻炼一下的话，\n『勉强』到底是个什么程度，\n此时此刻我是无法预测…%K%P
I was so overjoyed to have the cast removed that I jumped\nout of my hospital bed right away and ended up landing on\nmy bum. Asami nearly had a heart attack.%K%P
毕竟刚把石膏取下来的时候，\n从诊察室的床上很有劲的想要下床，\n却咚得一声跪在地上，吓得麻实惊声大叫。%K%P
